{
  "name": "std-agent-trace",
  "description": "std-agent-trace — the persisted record of what an in-app assistant did. Each REPLIED (from std-agent-tool-loop) stores one AgentRun row: the reply, every tool step (which input or entity, the arguments, whether it took effect and why not), the tokens and the model calls; each REPLY_FAILED stores a failed run with its error. The record verification grades and later optimisation reads, in one format for tests and production. AgentTraceRecorder is headless; AgentRunBrowse is the run list. Rows carry ownerId (the real @user); the binding organism scopes @read.",
  "level": "atom",
  "topic": "agent",
